{"type":"compaction","id":"cb7c158e","parentId":"e664f83a","timestamp":"2026-05-20T05:32:50.980Z","summary":"## Goal\n- Implementing a basic RESTful API using Flask\n- Integrating user authentication using Flask-Login\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Use Flask framework\n- Implement user authentication using Flask-Login\n- Store user data in a SQLite database\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Set up basic Flask API\n- [x] Install Flask-Login library\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Implement user registration and login routes\n\n### Blocked\n- [ ] Unable to persist user data in SQLite database due to incorrect table schema\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Use SQLAlchemy for database operations**: Due to ease of use and flexibility.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Correct the table schema in the SQLite database to persist user data correctly.\n2. Implement user registration and login routes using Flask-Login.\n3. Test user registration and login functionality.\n\n## Critical Context\n- User model class with fields for username, email, and password\n- SQLAlchemy table definition for user data\n- Flask-Login configuration for user authentication","firstKeptEntryId":"7c4bb028","tokensBefore":29110,"details":{"readFiles":[],"modifiedFiles":[]},"fromHook":false}
