{"type":"compaction","id":"3c9bf62c","parentId":"e1d5f578","timestamp":"2026-05-20T05:37:12.327Z","summary":"## Goal\n- Implementing a basic RESTful API using Flask\n- Integrating user authentication using Flask-Login\n- Handling user data validation for registration and login\n- Implementing password hashing using Flask-Bcrypt\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Use Flask framework\n- Implement user authentication using Flask-Login\n- Store user data in a SQLite database\n- Validate user input for registration and login\n- Use SQLAlchemy for database operations\n- Validate user input using WTForms\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Set up basic Flask API\n- [x] Install Flask-Login library\n- [x] Correct the table schema in the SQLite database to persist user data correctly\n- [x] Implement user registration route using Flask-Login\n- [x] Implement user login route using Flask-Login\n- [x] Test user registration and login functionality\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Implement user logout route using Flask-Login\n\n### Blocked\n- None\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Use SQLAlchemy for database operations**: Due to ease of use and flexibility.\n- **Validate user input using WTForms**: To ensure data integrity.\n- **Implement password hashing using Flask-Bcrypt**: For secure password storage.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Implement user logout route using Flask-Login.\n2. Implement password hashing using Flask-Bcrypt.\n3. Review and improve the overall security of the API.\n\n## Critical Context\n- User model class with fields for username, email, and password\n- SQLAlchemy table definition for user data\n- Flask-Login configuration for user authentication\n- WTForms form definition for user registration and login\n- Password hashing using Flask-Bcrypt","firstKeptEntryId":"7c4bb028","tokensBefore":29675,"details":{"readFiles":[],"modifiedFiles":[]},"fromHook":false}
